/*
   The OWASP Web Security Testing Guide, one guide per test case.

   Where the guides in knowledge.js are ours — written for a Top-10 category, with a
   pass criterion and the classic false positive called out — these are the
   published method itself: the summary and test objectives from the case page, and
   the steps OWASP prints under "How to Test". Quoting it rather than paraphrasing
   is the point: a client who asks "did you follow the WSTG?" should be able to
   open the same page and read the same instructions.

   Fetched from https://wstg.owasp.org/latest/<category>/<case>/ on 2026-11-24.
   Five cases the current edition dropped come from the WSTG repository's 4.2
   sources instead (File Extensions, RIA Cross Domain Policy, Weak Username Policy,
   Cross Site Flashing, and browser security controls for the header case), and
   WSTG-INFO-09 shares the framework page, whose own text says it was merged there.
   `items` lists the checklist sub items each guide answers, so the seed links them
   by case code rather than by guessing from the section.

   No `passes` and no `watch`: OWASP states neither, and inventing a pass criterion
   for 115 pages would be text nobody reviewed.
*/
