      'Alternative Authentication — Some applications will allow the user to prove their identity through other means, such as the use of security questions. This usually represents a significant weakness, as security questions provide a far lower level of security than MFA. The most common form of MFA is the one of One-Time Passwords (OTPs), which are typically six-digit numeric codes (although they can be longer or short…',
