      'Single Sign-On — If the application uses single sign-on, an expired application session may be renewed silently through the identity provider without asking the user for credentials. In that case, the lifetime of the identity provider session is the effective timeout, for both the idle and the absolute timeout. Measure it in the same way and report it, rather than only checking that the application issues a new sess…',
