      'Injection Detection — To detect CSTI, testers should inject characters that are syntactically significant to the template engine. The most common syntax for interpolation in many frameworks is double curly braces {% raw %}{{ }}{% endraw %}. A simple arithmetic operation is the standard probe. If the application evaluates the math, it is vulnerable. Generic Probe:',
